{"kind":"artifact","text":"The GitHub connector's inbound half at 6ca1266b21306cb96726d345eac9021a91488fe7 on request/github-connector-observe. The clauses bound the read: Fetch dispatches per clause, so a selection clause costs one request per issue it names and a criteria clause one bounded walk of what matches, and nothing enumerates the tracker. Labels ride on the issue, so a criteria clause cannot be defeated by a caller omitting them. The charter must name the connector, owner, repository and actor, and a body naming none of them is refused. Observations rest on the charter and the admitting clause, so retiring a clause flares what it let in.","body":{"commit":"6ca1266b21306cb96726d345eac9021a91488fe7","path":"request/github-connector-observe"}}